  "text": "We need to find the expected number of tosses of a fair coin until we get two heads in a row (HH).\n\nLet me set up the state equations. We define states based on the \"progress\" toward getting HH:\n\n- State 0: No relevant progress (we're at the start, or the last toss was a tail, or we just started — actually we need to be careful). Let me define states by what happened at the end of the sequence so far:\n  - State S₀: We have no consecutive heads going (i.e., the last toss was a tail, or no tosses yet).\n  - State S₁: The last toss was a head (so one more head gives us HH).\n  - State S₂: We've achieved HH (absorbing state).\n\nLet E₀ = expected number of additional tosses to reach HH given we're in state S₀.\nLet E₁ = expected number of additional tosses to reach HH given we're in state S₁.\n\nFrom state S₀: We toss the coin.\n- With probability 1/2, we get a head → move to state S₁. Then expected additional tosses is E₁.\n- With probability 1/2, we get a tail →",
